          tip: 'The descent from Alto del Perdón is steep loose gravel — trekking poles are invaluable here. Many knee injuries on the Camino happen on this downhill section.',
        },
        {
          time: 'Afternoon',
          icon: '☀️',
          title: 'Puente la Reina & La Rioja Vineyards',
          text: 'Puente la Reina — "Queen\'s Bridge" — is where the various Camino routes converge. The 11th-century Romanesque bridge over the Arga River, built for pilgrims by Queen Doña Mayor, is one of medieval Europe\'s finest. Beyond Puente la Reina, the trail enters La Rioja — Spain\'s premier wine region. The path runs directly through vineyards where winemakers sometimes offer free tastings from their bodegas in exchange for a donation stamp in your credencial.',
